 An additional `scripts/factory_integrated_browser_smoke.py` performs actual
 Chromium clicks where localhost browsing is permitted. Existing saves are not
 created or modified by either acceptance harness (they use temporary fixtures).
+
+### ECON-02B2d5 — Built colony floors, walls and doors (2026-11-01)
+
+Physical structure construction is **inside the colony UI**, not a second application
+or a second writer. Start the same colony host and Python relay documented under
+ECON-02B2d4c4, create a colony outpost and manufacture real modules, then open
+`/viewer/interactive.html` and find **Colony structures** in the colony panel.
+
+A structural plan is a versioned plain-text batch. Example:
+
+```text
+sg-colony-structure-plan-v1
+1,0,0
+2,0,0
+4,1,0
+```
+
+`kind,x,y` uses `1` = floor cell, `2/3` = east/north wall edge, and
+`4/5` = east/north door edge. Floors require one real module; each wall and
+door requires two. Doors are initially shut and can be opened/closed via the
+colony panel. A plan is authorized first; each **Construct next** issues exactly
+one host-controlled, material-conserving simulation command. Partial progress,
+completed structure geometry, cancelled plans and door state survive a restart.
+Cancelling does not refund already built structures. Construction in one world
+cannot be concurrent with a standalone factory writer; the world writer lease
+rejects the other process.
+
+There are no factory-tier floor-plan area caps. Each plan is a bounded **batch**
+(maximum 512 steps), and players can submit further plans to extend the same
+site. The current safe coordinate encoding has an internal ±1,000,000 cell
+limit per axis; this is not a claimed unlimited-coordinate engine. Collision
+checks reject same-edge wall/door replacement, crossing installed conveyors
+and machines, and new equipment or conveyor routes obstructing structures.
+`structure_edge_passable(...)` is authoritative geometry logic for later NPC
+movement integration, **not yet an operational NPC pathfinder**.
+
+Native tests and actual HTTP/SQLite recovery:
+
+```sh
+cmake --build build -j4
+ctest --test-dir build -j4 --output-on-failure
+node --test tests/*.js
+python scripts/colony_structures_browser_smoke.py  # optional Playwright + Chromium
+```
+
+The browser smoke injects a mock transport and exercises the real DOM controls;
+`galaxy_econ02b2d5_structure_host_http` independently tests the actual
+localhost server, simulation commands and persistent world. A real Chromium
+localhost interaction remains an acceptance gate when the browser permits it.
+Windows GUI/native verification remains outstanding.
